cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the dissertation it was written for."
title: "Machine Learning-Based Downscaling of GCM Outputs for Solar Energy Suitability Mapping over Zimbabwe"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for an MSc dissertation downscaling CMIP6 surface solar radiation
  to 0.1 degrees over Zimbabwe, benchmarking four machine learning architectures
  against a withheld ERA5 record, projecting to 2100 under two SSP pathways, and
  carrying the result into a multi-criteria suitability assessment for
  utility-scale photovoltaic development.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Chiagozie Raphael"
    family-names: "Madukwe"
    affiliation: "Department of Space Science and Applied Physics, University of Zimbabwe"
keywords:
  - statistical downscaling
  - CMIP6
  - solar irradiance
  - machine learning
  - multi-criteria evaluation
  - Zimbabwe
  - reproducibility
